Problem 5: Started coding a new feature and made 3 commits on main branch instead of a feature branch.
Commands:
git branch new-feature: creates a new branch pointing to these commits
git reset HEAD~3 --hard: rolls back main branch by 3 commits
git checkout new-feature: switches working path to the new feature branch

Problem 6: Made changes and commits in a detached HEAD state.
Commands:
git switch -c recovery-branch: creates a new branch right where you are to save floating commits